# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# There was no .dockerignore before this — every `docker build` copied the
# ENTIRE repo (via `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile's runtime stage) into the
# image, including .venv/ (600MB+), .git/ (full history, incl. a redacted
# pre-redact backup ref), and .env (real API keys — a secrets-in-image leak).
# That bloat is also what exhausted the host's disk across repeated builds.

.git/
.venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.github/
.claude/
.wolf/
.local/
docs/
*.md

tests/fixtures/challenge_mirror/.git/
